Three sons of slain Iranian leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei prayed beside his coffin and those of four other family members on Sunday, but Mojtaba, the son who has succeeded him as Iran's supreme leader, ​did not make ‌an appearance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef8054e8-785f-11f1-a2eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-05T102559Z-2125512687-RC2M7MAIW1PK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-KHAMENEI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef8054e8-785f-11f1-a2eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-05T102559Z-2125512687-RC2M7MAIW1PK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-KHAMENEI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ec282a4-7849-11f1-9c29-79bdaaae159b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 16:07:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef8054e8-785f-11f1-a2eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-05T102559Z-2125512687-RC2M7MAIW1PK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-KHAMENEI.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Summit host Turkey eyes major weapons deals with NATO allies</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260705-summit-host-turkey-eyes-major-weapons-deals-with-nato-allies</link><description>
